      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2000 European Federation of Chapters of the International Association for the Study of Pain.",
        "AbstractText": "In order to analyse the effects of potent exogenous analgesia with opioids in borderline personality disorder (BPD), we present a case report in which the application of morphine abolished the perception of pain during self-injury and intensified self-injurious activities. On the basis of our observations, we concluded that the use of potent analgesics might aggravate psychopathology in BPD."
      },
